Levels: Standards

Purpose:
  Defines project and entity complexity levels L0-L5.

ProjectLevels:
  L0:
    Name: Prototype
    Description: Minimal viable product
    Gates: Minimal checks
    Context: minimal
  L1:
    Name: Small project
    Description: Simple application
    Gates: Basic test + lint
    Context: low
  L2:
    Name: Production application
    Description: Production-ready with security
    Gates: Security + integration + deployment
    Context: medium
  L3:
    Name: Business-critical
    Description: High availability required
    Gates: Performance + security + observability
    Context: high
  L4:
    Name: High-scale
    Description: Millions of users
    Gates: Resilience + DR + advanced security
    Context: critical
  L5:
    Name: Mission-critical
    Description: Formal controls required
    Gates: Formal controls + continuous verification
    Context: exhaustive

EntityLevels:
  L0:
    Simple helper, utility
  L1:
    Basic feature
  L2:
    Business feature
  L3:
    Critical business feature
  L4:
    System-critical feature
  L5:
    Security/Compliance critical

LevelRules:
  [LV1]  Project level determines required gates.
  [LV2]  Entity level determines documentation depth.
  [LV3]  Higher levels include all lower level requirements.

State: +
  
